{
  "README": [
    "GOLDEN FIXTURE — Scope 1 (T5.2, TEST-3, О-11).",
    "",
    "A FIXED activity set and a FIXED factor set, with the expected kgCO2e for",
    "every row. Every expectation in `expectedLines[].arithmetic` was worked out",
    "BY HAND from the formulas of spec §9 (CALC-1/2/3/4) — not by running the",
    "engine and recording what it printed, and not by comparing against the",
    "deleted legacy calculator (О-11). The arithmetic string IS the proof: a",
    "reader can check any line here with a pencil, without trusting the code.",
    "",
    "THE FACTOR VALUES ARE FIXTURE DATA, not the shipped `legacy-v1` set. Most",
    "are the real DEFRA-shaped numbers so the magnitudes read as plausible; two",
    "are chosen for checkable arithmetic and say so on the row.",
    "",
    "VERSION HISTORY OF THIS FILE. It was written against hosmos-calc-1.0.0.",
    "T5.3 moved the version to 1.1.0 by adding CALC-5's market-based matching",
    "to the definition, and NOT ONE NUMBER BELOW CHANGED: nothing in the",
    "Scope-1 formula, the factor ladder, the year rule, the tie-break, the",
    "conversion preference or the rounding rule was touched, so the hand",
    "arithmetic still proves the same figures. Only the string was rewritten —",
    "which is exactly the review the pin below exists to force.",
    "",
    "1.2.0 DID touch the factor ladder: the `supplier_specific` rung now",
    "requires the factor's own `supplier_name` to be the SAME seller as the",
    "activity row's supplier (migration 0007), where before it admitted any",
    "`source_name='supplier'` row for any row naming any supplier. AND AGAIN",
    "NOT ONE NUMBER BELOW CHANGED, for a reason the fixture makes checkable:",
    "no factor here is supplier-sourced and no row here names a supplier, so",
    "every line below resolves on the `site_country`/`global` rungs, which the",
    "change does not touch. The rung it does touch is exercised by",
    "`scope2-dual.json` (ea05) — where the number is likewise unchanged,",
    "because the fixture's supplier factor now NAMES the seller that row buys",
    "from. Only the version string moved here.",
    "",
    "1.3.0 INSERTED A RUNG in the middle of the ladder — unit distance, between",
    "geography and the contextual/universal basis: a factor priced in the",
    "quantity the row was ENTERED in (same unit, or one `unit_conversion`",
    "renames it onto at exactly ×1) now beats any factor reached by a",
    "conversion that changes the number. Unlike 1.1.0 and 1.2.0 this one DOES",
    "move shipped figures — over `legacy-v1` it changes exactly two answers, a",
    "gas bill in `kWh` (FACTORS_AMBIGUOUS → the Gross-CV factor at ×1) and an",
    "LPG bill in `kWh` (the per-litre factor via a density round trip → the",
    "per-kWh factor at ×1) — so every line below was re-checked against the",
    "new ladder rather than assumed unaffected.",
    "NOT ONE NUMBER BELOW CHANGED, and the fixture makes the reason",
    "checkable without running anything:",
    "  - `conversions` here holds m³→kWh_gross (×11.0342), kg↔t (×0.001/×1000)",
    "    and L→m³ (×0.001). NONE of them is ×1, so no row can be promoted to",
    "    the `as_entered` rung by a renaming;",
    "  - `factors` holds exactly ONE factor per `activityType` (f1…f9), so no",
    "    row has two candidates for the new rung to reorder. a1 still reaches",
    "    f1 through the contextual m³→kWh_gross ×11.0342 (it is the only factor",
    "    natural gas has here); aa still reaches f9 by the identity, which was",
    "    already the nearest rung there is.",
    "Only the version string moved here. The rung is proved where it BITES, on",
    "the real 440-row `legacy-v1` set, in `calc/__tests__/factors.test.ts`.",
    "",
    "1.4.0 GAVE THE CONVERSION BASIS A SCOPE: migration 0010 put a",
    "`factor_set_id` on `unit_conversion`, and a row belonging to the period's",
    "PINNED set now outranks a shared one (`factor_set_id IS NULL`) whatever",
    "their bases — contextual still beating universal inside each scope. It",
    "moves shipped figures elsewhere: a Slovenian gas bill in `kWh` under",
    "`si-2025` was being priced through DEFRA's UK calorific values, whose two",
    "routes disagreed by 3.69% and tied into FACTORS_AMBIGUOUS, and is now",
    "priced through ARSO's own. NOT ONE NUMBER BELOW CHANGED, and the fixture",
    "makes the reason checkable with no code: EVERY conversion here carries",
    "`\"factorSetId\": null`, i.e. every one of them is a SHARED row, and the",
    "period pins a set that owns none — so all four sit on exactly the two",
    "rungs (`contextual`, `universal`) they sat on under 1.3.0, in the same",
    "order, and a1 still reaches f1 through m³→kWh_gross ×11.0342. Only the",
    "version string moved here.",
    "",
    "`formulaVersion`, `roundingRule` and `roundingDecimals` are part of the",
    "expectations on purpose: changing FORMULA_VERSION without revisiting these",
    "numbers must fail the suite, because the version is defined (see",
    "`calc/formula-version.ts`) to cover the formula, the factor ladder, the year",
    "rule, the tie-break, the conversion preference and the rounding rule — every",
    "one of which can move a figure below without an input changing.",
    "",
    "COVERAGE, per the T5.2 acceptance:",
    "  - all five Scope-1 categories (a1 a7 a8 a9 aa stationary, a2 mobile,",
    "    a3 a4 fugitive, a5 process, a6 onsite generation);",
    "  - both mass-balance branches (a3 mass_balance, a4 engineering_estimate);",
    "  - a biogenic row whose figure is ABSENT from the fossil total (a7 by the",
    "    factor's biogenic_treatment, a8 by the row's biogenic_flag);",
    "  - a row needing a unit conversion (a1, m³ → kWh_gross, contextual);",
    "  - a row with no factor: a9 carries `failed_missing_factor` and a NULL",
    "    result — never a 0 (§0.7, AC-6);",
    "  - a 15-significant-digit row (aa) whose exact product lands EXACTLY on the",
    "    6-decimal rounding boundary, so a float implementation gets it wrong;",
    "  - CALC-1's four rejections (b1…b5 in `rows`, listed in `expectedExcluded`).",
    "",
    "1.5.0 normalises factor output units to kgCO2e before final rounding.",
    "Every factor here already outputs kgCO2e; all hand-worked numbers are unchanged."
  ],

